#~ msgid "Decimal Mode Flag: Set when processor is in BCD (Binary Coded Decimal) mode. In this mode, arithmetic operations work with decimal numbers instead of binary. Rarely used in most applications."
#~ msgstr "十进制模式标志（D）：当处理器处于 BCD（二进制编码十进制）模式时置位。在此模式下，算术运算使用十进制数而非二进制数。在大多数应用中很少使用。"

#~ msgid "Each of these strips is 32 bytes long, and the value of the least significant byte of the memory location tells you how far along the row you are. For example, <tt>$0200</tt> is the first pixel of the first row, <tt>$0201</tt> is the second pixel of the first row, and so on. <tt>$021f</tt> is the last pixel of the first row. <tt>$0220</tt> is the first pixel of the second row, and so on."
#~ msgstr "每条带长 32 字节，内存位置的低位字节告诉你在行中的位置。例如，<tt>$0200</tt> 是第一行的第一个像素，<tt>$0201</tt> 是第一行的第二个像素，依此类推。<tt>$021f</tt> 是第一行的最后一个像素。<tt>$0220</tt> 是第二行的第一个像素，依此类推。"

#~ msgid "Each segment of the snake is two bytes: an x-coordinate and a y-coordinate. The segments are stored in order from head to tail. The head is stored at <tt>$10</tt> and <tt>$11</tt>, the first body segment at <tt>$12</tt> and <tt>$13</tt>, and the tail at <tt>$14</tt> and <tt>$15</tt>."
#~ msgstr "蛇的每段占两个字节：x 坐标与 y 坐标。段按从头到尾的顺序存储。头部存储在 <tt>$10</tt> 与 <tt>$11</tt>，第一身体段在 <tt>$12</tt> 与 <tt>$13</tt>，尾部在 <tt>$14</tt> 与 <tt>$15</tt>。"

#~ msgid "Each time a byte is pushed onto the stack, the stack pointer is decremented. Each time a byte is popped off the stack, the stack pointer is incremented."
#~ msgstr "每次有字节压入栈时，栈指针递减。每次有字节弹出栈时，栈指针递增。"

#~ msgid "Eight-bit processors are pretty fun. You might think that having such a small word size would be limiting, but actually it's not. It's quite interesting to see how much you can do with just 8 bits. And once you understand 8-bit processors, you'll understand the 6502 processor that powered many classic games and computers."
#~ msgstr "8 位处理器很有趣。你可能认为如此小的字长会有限制，但实际上不会。看到仅用 8 位能做多少事会很有趣。一旦你理解了 8 位处理器，就会理解驱动许多经典游戏与计算机的 6502 处理器。"
